{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most critical initial question is whether the basic multimodal pipeline (combining RNA and image features) is viable and what performance floor it establishes. config_001 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the simplest multimodal configuration: it uses standard, well-understood encoders (PCA for RNA, ResNet50 for image) and the most straightforward fusion (concatenation) with a single profile. This isolates the fundamental question of whether combining two modalities is informative at all, without confounding from learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, or weighted fusion. Its result will serve as a reference point for every subsequent comparison: if it performs well, we can test whether better encoders (scgpt, scvi), multiprofile aggregation, or weighted fusion add value; if it underperforms, we can diagnose whether the bottleneck is the encoder choice, the fusion strategy, or the modality combination itself. As the first experiment, establishing this simple multimodal baseline maximizes the interpretability of all future comparisons and reduces the largest source of uncertainty—whether the multimodal design space is worth exploring in depth."
}

